{
  "name": "customer",
  "main": "./src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-04-01",
// No flag here enables runtime `new Function()`, and that is deliberate.
//
// `packages/schema-registry` validates with `ajv.compile()`, which generates the
// validator from a string. Workers forbids it — `EvalError: Code generation from
// strings disallowed for this context` — and there is no way around it: the
// nearest flag, `allow_eval_during_startup`, only covers module startup, and the
// compile happens per request inside the route handler.
//
// An earlier attempt enabled a flag named `unsafe-eval` here. The deploy rejected
// it: `No such compatibility flag`. It was worth recording because the failure
// mode is the instructive one — the config is not validated by `pnpm -r typecheck`
// or by any test, only by a deploy, so an invented flag reads as correct locally.
//
// The consequence for this worker is handled in `routes.ts`, not here: a
// registration that has already been inserted reports the customer, and reports
// the event separately. If Ajv is ever replaced by a validator that does not
// codegen, `validate()` starts running again and the error log in that handler
// stops firing.
"compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "vars": {},
  "kv_namespaces": [
    {
      "binding": "SCHEMA_REGISTRY",
      "id": "732ccde5b0944db082d07667aba8104b"
    }
  ],
  "queues": {
    "producers": [
      {
        "binding": "DOMAIN_EVENTS_QUEUE",
        "queue": "vyloop-domain-events"
      }
    ]
  }
,
  "observability": { "enabled": true, "head_sampling_rate": 1 }
}